# Sourced by ~/scripts/tmux-sessionizer (its hydrate() function) into the first
# window of a *newly created* session -- not when switching to one that already
# exists, so this runs once per project.
#
# tmux created the window with -c <project>, so the cwd is already the selected
# project and `nvim .` lands in it.
#
# Any project can override this by dropping its own .tmux-sessionizer at its
# root; hydrate() prefers the project-local file over this one.

nvim .
